-- title:
--   Transport of the Drinfeld Γ(q)-pair is relabelling by γ
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'\ge 1$ is a natural number with $q\nmid M'$ (hypothesis `hqM'`), and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ (hypotheses `hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`). The field $L$ has characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity, and `hιξ` asserts that some ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ satisfies $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell_g)}$. The subgroup $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is required by `hH₁` to be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ is required by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the image of the rational function field `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁` $\subseteq \mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ under the coefficientwise extension [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) along $\mathbb Q\to L$. Further, $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ lying in its maximal ideal (`hAq`), and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$; the element $j\in K$ has image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) in $L((\mathsf q))$, the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function, and $j\neq 0$. The hypotheses `hℓA` and `hM'A` say that $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units in $A$.
--
--   The moduli frame consists of the following groups of hypotheses. Equivariance pins: `hℓ` says that for every $A$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData` $D$, `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` implies `IsGamma1Point (C • W) ℓg (D.variableChange C)`; `hM` says that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` implies `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k (kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h)`; `hL` says that if $h$ divides `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` then `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` divides `inLineMulPoly (C • W) ℓg n (u^{-2}(x-r))` for the data $u=C.u$, $r=C.r$. Group-law pins: $\mathcal G$ is a family of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models over $A$-algebras with unit discriminant, `h𝒢` asserting that each is realised by a points-evaluation (chord–tangent), `h𝒢O` that its unit section is cut out by an origin chart with $x/y$ and $z/y$ going to $0$. Transport pins: $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport A 𝒢 q` and `h𝒯` says it is a section transport, i.e. its `act` and `map` operations carry the sections of a raw Drinfeld pair to the expected sections after a variable change, respectively after a coefficient change. Realisation pins: `hVC` provides, for every $A$-algebra $T$, projective Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ and variable change $C$, a graded ring homomorphism `projModelGradingCR W →+*ᵍ projModelGradingCR (C • W)` satisfying the irrelevant-ideal inclusion and `IsVariableChangeHom W C`; `hCO` provides the analogous homomorphism along an $A$-algebra map $f$, satisfying `IsCoefficientHom W f`.
--
--   With these data, `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯` is the rigid Weierstrass datum over $A$ whose level structure is the product of: a family of polynomials indexed by the prime factors $p$ of $M'$ with `IsGamma0PowAt W p (M'.factorization p)`; a `LevelPData` $D$ with `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` (the point $(x_P,y_P)$ lies on $W$, $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g})(x_P)=0$, and $x_Q=x_P$, $y_Q=y_P$); and a raw Drinfeld pair with the $\Gamma(q)$-level condition relative to $\mathcal G$ and $\mathcal T$; all this restricted to tuples satisfying `IsGamma1Link W ℓg M'`, namely that if $\ell_g$ is a prime factor of $M'$ then the $\ell_g$-component polynomial divides `inLineMulPoly W ℓg (ℓg ^ (M'.factorization ℓg - 1)) x_P`. Accordingly $x$ is a raw datum of this level structure over $K$: a Weierstrass curve `x.curve` with unit discriminant, the level tuple `x.level` whose components are written `x.level.1`, `x.level.2.1` (the `LevelPData`) and `x.level.2.2` (the raw Drinfeld pair, with projective curve `x.level.2.2.curve` and sections `x.level.2.2.P`, `x.level.2.2.Q`), together with the proof that the tuple is a level structure on `x.curve`. Finally $C_0$ is a variable change over $L((\mathsf q))$.
--
--   Write $(x_c,y_c)$ for the pair of Laurent series [`ModularCurve.tateToricPoint L q c`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelPCusps.html#L20) attached to a unit $c$ of $L$, and $\zeta$ for the $q$-th power of the unit of $L$ determined by $\xi$ (a primitive $\ell_g$-th root of unity); $\mathrm C(a)$ denotes the constant Hahn series with value $a$. The hypothesis `hx` is the conjunction of five clauses. First, the variable change is normalised: $C_0.u\cdot(2x_\zeta+\mathrm C(1/6))=2y_\zeta+x_\zeta$, $C_0.r=\mathrm C(-1/12)$, $C_0.s=\mathrm C(-1/2)$ and $C_0.t=\mathrm C(1/24)$. Secondly, the base change of `x.curve` along $K\to L((\mathsf q))$ equals $C_0\bullet$[`ModularCurve.tateBase L q`](def/ModularCurve_TateSlots.html#L46). Thirdly, the image of `x.level.2.1` under the coefficient map $K\to L((\mathsf q))$ equals the $C_0$-variable change of the `LevelPData` $\langle x_\zeta,y_\zeta,x_\zeta,y_\zeta\rangle$. Fourthly, there are $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y\in K$ whose images in $L((\mathsf q))$ are, respectively, the four coordinates `xP`, `yP`, `xQ`, `yQ` of the $C_0$-variable change of [`ModularCurve.cuspData L q (ξ^{ℓ_g}) ![1, 0] ![0, -1]`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelPCusps.html#L71) (so the $P$-coordinates come from the toric point with parameter the primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi^{\ell_g}$, and the $Q$-coordinates from the non-toric branch `nonToricPoint` for the vector $(0,-1)$), and such that `IsSectionThrough x.level.2.2.P Px Py` and `IsSectionThrough x.level.2.2.Q Qx Qy` hold, i.e. each section is realised by a ring homomorphism out of the $Z$-chart ring sending the affine coordinates to the indicated values. Fifthly, the image in $L((\mathsf q))$ of the $j$-invariant `jOf (Quot.mk _ x)` of the class of $x$ in the level moduli datum of the rigid datum equals [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the $q$-expansion `qExpand L q (jqModC L)`.
--
--   Next, $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lies in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ is an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ subject to [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q (ξ ^ ℓg) q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k\in\mathbb Z$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) viewed inside $GL_2(\mathbb R)$, every pair of integral power series $p_f,p_g$ with `IsIntegralQExp f pf`, `IsIntegralQExp g pg` and `intSeriesC ℚ pg ≠ 0`, every $y\in K$ whose image in $L((\mathsf q))$ is the coefficient extension of the ratio `intSeriesC ℚ pf / intSeriesC ℚ pg`, and every ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi^{\ell_g})=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of $\tau(y)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\,$`conjElemN q γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k\,$`conjElemN q γ⁻¹`, where `conjElemN q δ` is the matrix with rows $(\delta_{00},\delta_{01}/q)$ and $(q\delta_{10},\delta_{11})$.
--
--   The unit $\mu\in K^\times$ is subject to `hμ`: writing $a=\gamma_{00}\in\mathbb Z$ and $\zeta^a$ for the $a$-th power of $\zeta$, the identity
--   $$\mu\,(2y_{\zeta^a}+x_{\zeta^a})\cdot 2\,(x_{\zeta}+\mathrm C(1/12))=(2y_{\zeta}+x_{\zeta})\cdot 2\,(x_{\zeta^a}+\mathrm C(1/12))$$
--   holds in $L((\mathsf q))$. Finally `hc` requires that the Weierstrass curve of the datum obtained by transporting $x$ along the $A$-algebra homomorphism underlying $\tau$ (`mapRing`) and then acting by the variable change $\langle\mu,0,0,0\rangle$ equals `x.curve`.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion asserts that the discriminant of the projective curve `x.level.2.2.curve` is a unit, and that for the corresponding proof $h_\Delta$ the Drinfeld component of the transported and rescaled datum, that is the `level.2.2` component of `act ⟨μ, 0, 0, 0⟩ (mapRing τ x)`, is equal to [`ModularCurve.LevelRelabelling.RawDrinfeldPair.relabel 𝒢 γ x.level.2.2 hΔ`](def/ModularCurve_LevelRelabelling.html#L53): the raw Drinfeld pair on the same projective curve `x.level.2.2.curve` whose first section is `zlinComb (𝒢 K x.level.2.2.curve hΔ) P Q γ₀₀ γ₁₀` and whose second section is `zlinComb (𝒢 K x.level.2.2.curve hΔ) P Q γ₀₁ γ₁₁`, where $P$ and $Q$ are the sections of `x.level.2.2` and `zlinComb G P Q a b` is the product under $G$ of the $a$-fold multiple of $P$ and the $b$-fold multiple of $Q$. Note that the automorphism $\tau$ is pinned by $\gamma^{-1}$, while the relabelling in the conclusion is by the matrix of $\gamma$.
--
--   This is the Drinfeld-level half of the comparison between the Galois-type automorphism $\tau$ of the $H_1$-level modular function field attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and the matrix action on level structures: it identifies the transported $\Gamma(q)$-basis with the $\gamma$-relabelling of the original basis, the computation being pinned at the Tate curve and its toric and non-toric cusp points. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_variableChange_act_mapRing_eq_relabel_of_isLevelAutAt_of_level_fst_rigidDataH1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_variableChange_act_mapRing_eq_relabel_of_isLevelAutAt_of_level_fst_rigidDataH1Pow), where the diamond action on the moduli problem of level $H_1$ is assembled from the separate level components.
